<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105501" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροπαία</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνοή</span>), ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>an alternating wind,</i> esp. <i>one which
				blows back from sea to land,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπογεία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				940b22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				945a6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Vent.</u>
				31
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				53
			</span></i>; <i>tropaei</i> (<i>venti</i>), <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				2.114
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ.</span> is said to have meant
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἐναντία πνοή</span> in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1103
			</span></i> (where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριπαία, τρίπαια,
			τριπαῖα</span> codd.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λήματος, φρενὸς
				τροπαία,</span>
			<i>a change in the spirit</i> of one's heart or mind, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				706
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				219
			</span></i> (both lyr.); but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. κακῶν</span>
			<i>a change from, release from</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				775
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
